I have the complete picture. Here is the detailed report.

---

# Slash-Command Menu — Full Investigation

## 0. Framework confirmation

**Qwik 2**, beta. `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/package.json`:
- `"@builder.io/qwik": "npm:@qwik.dev/core@2.0.0-beta.42"` (alias), plus direct `"@qwik.dev/core": "2.0.0-beta.42"`.
- Editor files import from `"@qwik.dev/core"` directly (not the alias).
- Editor is **TipTap 3 / ProseMirror** inside a Qwik `component$`.
- Test runner: **`bun test`** — `"test": "bun test --conditions=production --preload ./tests/qwik-test-preload.ts"`. The preload (`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/tests/qwik-test-preload.ts`) stubs `globalThis.__EXPERIMENTAL__` because Bun imports Qwik source directly without the Vite feature-table replacement. Note `vitest ^4.1.10` is also a devDependency (used by Storybook), but **every editor test file imports `from "bun:test"`**.

---

## 1. `src/components/editor/slash-command-menu.tsx` (241 lines)

### Props (lines 17–27)
```ts
interface SlashCommandMenuProps {
  open: boolean;
  query: string;
  context?: EditorCommandContext;
  platform?: ShortcutPlatform;
  /** Fixed viewport coordinates supplied by the TipTap integration. */
  left: number;
  top: number;
  onSelect$: PropFunction<(commandId: EditorCommandId) => void>;
  onClose$: PropFunction<() => void>;
}
```
Only `left`/`top` are supplied — **there is no `width`, `height`, `maxHeight`, or placement prop**, and no way for the parent to express "flip above".

### Exported pure helpers (unit-tested)
- `reconcileSlashSelection(candidates, selectedCommandId)` — lines 36–47. Keeps selection pinned to a **command ID**, falls back to `candidates[0]`, returns `null` for an empty set.
- `moveSlashSelection(candidates, selectedCommandId, direction)` — lines 50–63. Wraps modulo `candidates.length`.
- `optionId(commandId)` — line 65, sanitises the ID into `slash-command-<id>` for `aria-activedescendant`.

### Active-index tracking (lines 71–80)
**There is no numeric index.** Selection is a `useSignal<SlashSelectionId>(null)` holding an `EditorCommandId | null`:
```ts
const selectedCommandId = useSignal<SlashSelectionId>(null);
const candidates: SlashCommandCandidate[] = fuzzySlashCommands(
  props.query, props.context, props.platform ?? "mac",
);
const visibleSelection = reconcileSlashSelection(candidates, selectedCommandId.value);
```
`candidates` is recomputed **synchronously in the render body** on every re-render (not `useComputed$`).

### Keyboard handling (lines 82–141) — `useVisibleTask$`
```ts
// eslint-disable-next-line qwik/no-use-visible-task
useVisibleTask$(({ cleanup, track }) => {
  const open = track(() => props.open);
  const query = track(() => props.query);
  const currentCandidates = fuzzySlashCommands(query, props.context, props.platform ?? "mac");
  selectedCommandId.value = reconcileSlashSelection(currentCandidates, selectedCommandId.value);
  if (!open) return;

  const onKeyDown = (event: KeyboardEvent) => { /* Escape / ArrowDown / ArrowUp / Enter */ };
  window.addEventListener("keydown", onKeyDown, true);   // ← line 139, CAPTURE phase
  cleanup(() => window.removeEventListener("keydown", onKeyDown, true));
});
```
Key facts:
- Listener is on **`window`, capture phase (`true`)**, not on the menu element. This is what makes the menu work while the caret stays in ProseMirror.
- The task **re-runs on every keystroke** (it tracks `props.query`), so the listener is torn down and re-added per character.
- `props.context` and `props.platform` are read **untracked** inside the task.
- Inside the handler, candidates are **re-derived at keypress time** (lines 105–109) with the deliberate comment: *"A rapid query change must never leave Enter acting on the candidate array from the prior render."*
- `event.preventDefault()` is called for Escape/ArrowDown/ArrowUp/Enter, but **`stopPropagation()` is never called**. This happens to be safe — see §3 note on ProseMirror's `eventBelongsToView`.
- `Enter` guards `event.isComposing` (line 126). Arrow keys do **not**.
- Only `ArrowDown`/`ArrowUp` are handled — no `Home`/`End`/`PageUp`/`PageDown`/`Tab`.
- `if (visibleCandidates.length === 0) return;` (line 110) sits **after** the Escape branch, so Escape still closes an empty menu.

### DOM refs
**None.** There is no `useSignal<HTMLElement>()`, no `ref={}` attribute anywhere in the file. The root `<div>`, the scroll container, and the option `<button>`s are all unreferenced.

### scrollIntoView
**Absent.** Grep across `src/` shows `scrollIntoView` in `document-outline.tsx:52`, `twyne-editor.tsx:1936` and `:3382`, `comments-panel.tsx:217`, `personas-panel.tsx:1142`, `find-replace.ts`, `note-editing.ts`, `section-reorder.ts` — but **never** in `slash-command-menu.tsx`. Arrowing past the visible window of the `max-h-80` scroller moves `aria-activedescendant` and the highlight but the row stays off-screen.

### Positioning (lines 143–159)
```tsx
if (!props.open) return null;

return (
  <div
    class="fixed w-72 overflow-hidden border border-[var(--color-paper-3)] bg-[var(--color-paper)] shadow-lg"
    style={{
      left: `${props.left}px`,
      top: `${props.top}px`,
      zIndex: "var(--z-dropdown)",
      borderRadius: "2px",
    }}
    role="listbox"
    aria-label="Insert command"
    aria-activedescendant={visibleSelection ? optionId(visibleSelection) : undefined}
  >
```
- `position: fixed`, **top-left anchored only**. No `bottom`, no `right`, no `maxHeight`, **no clamping of `left` or `top` against the viewport**.
- Width fixed at `w-72` = **288px**.
- `--z-dropdown: 30` (`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/global.css:68`).
- I grepped `twyne-editor.tsx` for `transform` / `scale(` / `zoom`: only two hits at lines 402/406 inside a `useStyles$` keyframe-ish rule for a different element. **No ancestor establishes a containing block**, so `position: fixed` really is viewport-relative and matches `coordsAtPos` output. Good news for a fix — you can clamp purely in viewport space.

### Height budget (relevant to the off-screen bug)
- Header `<p>` (line 160): `px-3 py-2 text-[0.62rem]` ≈ **~29–33px**.
- List container (line 175): `class="max-h-80 overflow-y-auto py-1"` → **max 320px** + 8px padding.
- So the menu's max rendered height is roughly **~360px**, while `top` is set to `caretBottom + 6` with no upward flip. With a caret in the last ~360px of the viewport the menu hangs off the bottom.
- There are **21 slash commands** declared (`grep -c "    slash: {" src/utils/editor-commands.ts` → 21), so with an empty query the list is always at its `max-h-80` cap plus group headers.

### Item rendering (lines 167–237)
- Empty state: `"No commands match."` (line 172).
- Grouping is computed **inline during the map** (lines 177–179): a group header renders when `index === 0` or the previous candidate's group differs. `slashGroup()` (line 29) reads `candidate.command.slash?.group ?? "Commands"`. **Group headers are siblings inside the same wrapper `<div>` as the button**, so any scroll-into-view logic must target the `<button>`, not the wrapper, or the header will be scrolled instead.
- Each option is a `<button id={optionId(...)} role="option" aria-selected={isSelected}>`.
- Highlight is class-only: `bg-[var(--color-paper-2)] text-[var(--color-vermilion)]` vs `hover:bg-[var(--color-paper-soft)]`.
- `onMouseEnter$` sets `selectedCommandId.value` — mouse hover and keyboard share one selection signal (mouse movement over the list will fight arrow-key navigation once scrolling is added).
- `onMouseDown$={(event) => event.preventDefault()}` (line 205) — **this is the deliberate focus-retention mechanism**: it prevents the button from stealing focus from the contenteditable.
- `onClick$` calls `props.onSelect$(...)`.

### Focus — the actual behaviour
The menu is **never focused**. There is no `tabindex`, no `.focus()` call, no focus trap. Focus stays in `.ProseMirror` at all times; the menu is a purely visual overlay driven by a capture-phase window listener. Consequences:
- `role="listbox"` + `aria-activedescendant` are on a **non-focusable div**, so assistive tech never announces the active option. The correct ARIA combobox pattern would put `aria-activedescendant` / `aria-controls` / `aria-expanded` on the contenteditable host.
- Any other focused element in the page (e.g. the find/replace input, a panel textarea) will **also** be subject to the capture-phase handler — the handler does not check `event.target`. If the slash state somehow stays open while focus is in an `<input>`, Arrow/Enter there get hijacked.

---

## 2. `src/components/editor/popover-positioning.ts` (147 lines)

Pure math, **zero Qwik imports** — deliberately so, per the file header. Written for the persona-note popover and the margin card; **the slash menu does not import it.**

### Constants (lines 10–19)
```ts
export const POPOVER_CARD_WIDTH = 340;
export const POPOVER_CARD_MARGIN = 8;
export const MARGIN_CARD_GAP = 12;
export const POPOVER_CARD_IDEAL_HEIGHT = 520;
```
Note `POPOVER_CARD_WIDTH = 340` ≠ the slash menu's 288 (`w-72`) — any reuse needs a width parameter, which the current API does **not** accept (it's a module constant, not a field on `PopoverView`).

### Types (lines 21–56)
```ts
export type PopoverPlacement = "below" | "above";

export interface PopoverGeometry {
  x: number;
  top: number | null;      // null when bottom-anchored above
  bottom: number | null;   // null when top-anchored below
  maxH: number;
  placement: PopoverPlacement;
}

export interface AnchorRect { left: number; top: number; bottom: number }

export interface PopoverView {
  vw: number;
  vh: number;
  rect: AnchorRect;
  idealH?: number;   // defaults to POPOVER_CARD_IDEAL_HEIGHT
}

export interface MarginCardView extends PopoverView {
  page: { left: number; right: number };
}
```

### `computePopoverGeometry(view: PopoverView): PopoverGeometry` (lines 107–147)
**Yes — this is exactly the flip/clamp logic you want.** Documented rules at lines 94–106:
1. Prefer below (`rect.bottom + margin`).
2. Flip above **only** when `spaceBelow < idealH && spaceAbove > spaceBelow`. Ties fall through to below.
3. Clamp `maxH` to the winning side's space, so the card never overlaps the anchor.

```ts
const x = Math.max(margin, Math.min(view.rect.left, view.vw - POPOVER_CARD_WIDTH - margin));
const belowTop = view.rect.bottom + margin;
const aboveBottomCoord = view.rect.top - margin;
const spaceBelow = Math.max(0, view.vh - margin - belowTop);
const spaceAbove = Math.max(0, aboveBottomCoord - margin);
const flipAbove = spaceBelow < idealH && spaceAbove > spaceBelow;

if (flipAbove) {
  const maxH = Math.max(0, Math.min(idealH, spaceAbove));
  return { x, top: null, bottom: Math.max(0, view.vh - view.rect.top + margin), maxH, placement: "above" };
}
const maxH = Math.max(0, Math.min(idealH, spaceBelow));
return { x, top: belowTop, bottom: null, maxH, placement: "below" };
```
Deliberate design note (lines 100–103): the flipped card is **bottom-anchored** so it grows upward and doesn't jitter as content streams in. That reasoning applies to the slash menu too, where the list length changes as the query is typed.

**API limitation for your fix:** `POPOVER_CARD_WIDTH` is hard-coded inside the function. To reuse for a 288px menu you'd need to add an optional `width?: number` to `PopoverView` (defaulting to `POPOVER_CARD_WIDTH`) — a small, test-covered change.

### `computeMarginCardGeometry(view: MarginCardView)` (lines 64–92)
Right-margin-first, left-margin fallback, clamp-to-edge otherwise; always returns `placement: "below"` with a top clamped into `[margin, vh - maxH - margin]`. This is the one `twyne-editor.tsx` actually imports (line 169), used at lines 1126, 2042, 2381.

---

## 3. `src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx` (3450 lines)

### Imports (lines 169, 185–186)
```ts
import { computeMarginCardGeometry } from "./popover-positioning";
...
import { SlashCommand, getSlashCommandState } from "./extensions/slash-command";
import { SlashCommandMenu } from "./slash-command-menu";
```

### State — `useStore`, not signals (lines 258, 320–323)
```ts
const store = useStore<EditorStore>({ ... });
// ...
  slashOpen: false,
  slashQuery: "",
  slashLeft: 0,
  slashTop: 0,
```
Declared in `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/editor/editor-state.ts:143-146`:
```ts
slashOpen: boolean;
slashQuery: string;
slashLeft: number;
slashTop: number;
```
**Four flat numbers/strings — no placement, no maxHeight field.** A fix that adds flip/clamp needs new fields here (e.g. `slashPlacement`, `slashBottom`, `slashMaxH`) or a single `slashGeometry: PopoverGeometry | null`.

### Position computation — the off-screen bug (lines 1018–1032)
```ts
const refreshSlashMenu = () => {
  const slash = getSlashCommandState(editor.state);
  store.slashOpen = slash.open;
  store.slashQuery = slash.query;
  if (!slash.open) return;
  try {
    const coords = editor.view.coordsAtPos(slash.to);
    store.slashLeft = coords.left;
    store.slashTop = coords.bottom + 6;      // ← always below, never clamped, never flipped
  } catch {
    store.slashOpen = false;
  }
};
editor.on("transaction", refreshSlashMenu);
refreshSlashMenu();
```
This is **the single site to fix**. Observations:
- `coordsAtPos(slash.to)` returns **viewport coordinates** — directly compatible with `position: fixed`, and with `computePopoverGeometry`'s `rect`.
- Hard-coded `+ 6` gap (the popover module uses `POPOVER_CARD_MARGIN = 8`).
- `coords.left` is not clamped against `window.innerWidth - 288`, so a caret near the right edge also pushes the menu off-screen horizontally (a second, unreported bug in the same line).
- `coords` has `.top`, `.bottom`, `.left`, `.right` — everything `AnchorRect` needs (`{ left, top, bottom }`).
- **Bound only to `editor.on("transaction", ...)`.** I grepped for scroll/resize listeners in this file: the only hits are `onScrollToNote` / `onScrollToSuggestion` custom events (lines 1648, 1848). There is **no `window.addEventListener("scroll" | "resize")`** anywhere — so scrolling the manuscript while the menu is open leaves the menu frozen at stale viewport coordinates. Worth fixing alongside.
- Cleanup: `editor.off("transaction", refreshSlashMenu)` at **line 1915**, inside the big `cleanup(() => { ... })` of the editor-init `useVisibleTask$` (which begins at **line 488**).

