## Summary for your three fixes

**A. Off-screen at the bottom.** Single root cause at `twyne-editor.tsx:1024-1026`. `computePopoverGeometry` in `popover-positioning.ts:107` already implements flip+clamp and is fully tested; it needs an optional `width` field on `PopoverView` (currently hard-codes `POPOVER_CARD_WIDTH = 340` vs the menu's 288). Then `EditorStore` (`editor-state.ts:143-146`) needs `bottom`/`maxH`/`placement`, the props interface (`slash-command-menu.tsx:17-27`) needs to accept them, and the root div (line 146) needs to honour `bottom` + `maxHeight` instead of the fixed `max-h-80` on the inner scroller. `left` is unclamped horizontally too. Separately, nothing recomputes position on scroll/resize (no such listener exists in the file).

**B. Inconsistent keyboard focus.** The menu never takes focus by design (`onMouseDown$` preventDefault at line 205 keeps the caret in ProseMirror; the window capture listener at line 139 does all the work). The real inconsistencies are: (i) the global bubble-phase handler at `twyne-editor.tsx:1443-1481` is unaware of `store.slashOpen` and does not check `defaultPrevented`, so Escape and registry chords double-fire; (ii) the capture handler doesn't filter on `event.target`, so it acts even if focus is in an input; (iii) `selectSlashCommand` (line 2961) calls `editor.commands.focus()` *after* `runRegistryCommand`, which for the dialog-opening branches (`insert.image`, `insert.table`, `insert.mermaid`, notes) steals focus back from the dialog just opened; (iv) ARIA is broken — `aria-activedescendant` sits on an unfocusable `div`.

**C. No scrollIntoView.** There are **no refs at all** in the file. You need a `useSignal<HTMLElement | undefined>()` on the `max-h-80` scroll container (line 175) plus either per-option refs or a `querySelector(`#${optionId(sel)}`)` lookup, driven from a `useVisibleTask$` tracking `selectedCommandId.value`. Target the `<button>`, not its wrapper `<div>` (the wrapper also contains the group header). The house idiom for making this testable under `bun test` is `document-outline.tsx:38-53` + `document-outline.test.ts`.
